  "fields": {
    "responsibility": "One existing POSIX emulated word-service responsibility: actual mutex RMW, modulo bit-pattern semantics, standalone fence and real constructor/user/drain, integrated native tests.",
    "retired": "Signed-overflow compiler-option dependence and empty hope-for-the-best fence; unqualified queued fixture use of nonexistent sync-slot API; irrelevant thread formatting/name churn preserved as rejected bytes. Existing operation names and source mutex remain; no new runtime record/namespace.",
    "validation": "Actual parent strict UBSan max+1 overflow, candidate same diagnostic passes. Native and isolated emulated Make consumers run16384 locked updates,4096 atomic litmus rounds,trylock/wrap/CAS/clear and real module cleanup. No production archive linked into altered fallback ABI. Fresh SFUN204-action replay/shrink,7 constructor controls,GC/exception and processor1 pass. Existing root ticket QNT4 directed cases/1000 bounded traces. Same GSI/GSC/seed bytes and51 generated artifacts reused.",
    "benefits": "The service itself owns bit-pattern arithmetic and meaningful ordering rather than a compiler flag/no-op assumption. Two original queued paths close43\u219241; one of nine groups completes, eight remain nonempty. Primary production executable is byte-identical, with zero added runtime fields/allocations.",
    "costs": "C23 atomic support required; one real emulated dmb replaces no-op. Literal signed cast avoided via representation copy. Strict diagnostic uses test-only -fno-wrapv/UBSan, not production failure. Actual primary -fwrapv/config/profile preserved. A/A24 samples show label noise up to16.126% for1 arg, not speedup; no full CAS-less machine/32-bit/emulated Scheme VM qualification.",
    "process": "One complete three-path source/Make cut, not a single unchecked arithmetic edit. Old index prototypes retained by exact hashes and only those two entries replaced; all other staged bytes preserved. Shared test Make keeps future hunks. Independent SMP1/12 unchanged.",
    "checklist": "dev/refactoring/modern-c/ordered-fallback.org#ordered-word-fallback",
    "models": "Native OpenSysML SDK seven obligations/three real RMW/grant/fence adapters drives existing ASCENT missing/stale controls. Existing root QNT completion-order premise reused; its missing-order negative is not a current mutex-CAS bug. No duplicate Lean/protocol model. Normative C23 source and native emitted code do not prove all weak-memory executions.",
    "open": "Whole emulated Scheme VM, actual CAS-less compilers, non64-bit/other platform runtime, arbitrary races/dead-owner recovery, whole SMP and stable performance remain separate. Existing production builtin behavior was not signed-UB under its-fwrapv flag. Remote CI separate."
  },
